# GROKBOT-NESTED-BODY-WITNESSES-20260922-69 originally tested that an own
# declared inside a nested body is NOT reachable as node\name because node
# was a host-less spelling gate onto the CURRENT method's own table. Under
# FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-20260923-121, node\x means "field x of M.parent"
# (the unit, for any method other than E) -- host no longer matters, and
# neither does which method's body node\inner is written in: E's own
# fields are shared/int: shared below, not inner, so this still refuses,
# now as an ordinary unresolved segment on the unit rather than a
# host-filter rejection.
int: shared

fn: bad_node_inner () int
    if: 1
        int: inner 9
        node\inner: 5
    ---
    return: 0
end: bad_node_inner

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: bad_node_inner(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
